        "Antoine Georges",
        "Dieter Vollhardt",
        "Gabriel Kotliar"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Dynamical mean-field theory made strongly correlated electrons quantitatively tractable and transformed the interpretation of correlated materials.",
        "attribution": "Vollhardt and collaborators established the infinite-dimensional framework, while Georges and Kotliar made the modern method and its applications decisive.",
        "maturity": "Its predictions and computational framework have been tested and used extensively over several decades.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "Credit is distributed across a large theoretical community and between foundational formulation and later implementation."
        ]
      }
    },
